==========================================================================
  loaded 30 high-z galaxies with fDM
  redshift range: 0.58 - 1.68 (median 1.14)
  fDM range: 1.400 - 7.200 (median 3.200)

  fDM scatter, low-z half: 1.1165 (N=15)
  fDM scatter, high-z half: 1.5944 (N=15)
  [PASS] N3 [THE TREND, CRUDE] the high-z half shows LARGER fDM scatter than
      the low-z half -- the direction the evolving-partition
      prediction requires (weak evidence at this sample size)
         measured: scatter: low-z 1.1165 -> high-z 1.5944 (ratio 1.428)
         HONEST: 30 galaxies split in half is ~15 per bin, so this is a\n         DIRECTION, not a detection. The prediction is registered for\n         a proper test with the full high-z sample (and future larger\n         IFU surveys). What is established is the PREDICTION itself,\n         which is novel and quantitative: scatter grows as the inverse\n         phantom share.

